.TH WELLE-PI "1" "November 2026" "welle-pi 3.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
welle-pi \- welle.io interface for the Raspberry Pi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B welle-pi
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]
.br
.B welle-pi
\fI\,-b \/\fR[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
welle\-pi is welle.io's interface for Raspberry PI.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Tuning:"
.TP
\fB\-c\fR channel
Tune to <channel> (eg. 10B, 5A, 12C...).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR programme
Play <programme> with ALSA. The <programme> can be either
* a station's label (eg. GRIFF) \- or a part of it \- or
* a station's Service Id (eg. 0x4f57 or 20311).
.SS "Backend and input options:"
.TP
\fB\-f\fR file
Read an IQ file <file> and play with ALSA.
IQ file format is u8, unless the file ends with 'FORMAT.iq'.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR
Disable coarse corrector, for receivers who have a low
frequency offset.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR gain
Set input gain to <gain> or \fB\-1\fR for auto gain.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR driver
Set input driver and arguments.
Please note that some input drivers are available only if
they were enabled at build time.
Possible values are: auto (default), airspy, rtl_sdr,
android_rtl_sdr, rtl_tcp, soapysdr.
With "rtl_tcp", host IP and port can be specified as
"rtl_tcp,<HOST_IP>:<PORT>".
.TP
\fB\-s\fR args
SoapySDR Driver arguments.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR antenna
Set input antenna to ANT (for SoapySDR input only).
.SS "Output options:"
.TP
\fB\-o\fR device
Specify alsa PCM device by name.
.SS "Daemon options:"
.TP
\fB\-b\fR
Detach from the terminal and run in the background.
In that mode welle\-pi does not read commands from
standard input any more, it keeps playing the selected
programme until it receives SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR logfile
Append standard output and standard error to <logfile>.
Without this option they are sent to \fI\,/dev/null\/\fP when
running as a daemon.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR pidfile
Write the process id to <pidfile> and remove that file
again on exit.
.SS "Other options:"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Display this help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Output version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
welle\-pi \-c 10B \-p GRRIF
.IP
Receive 'GRRIF' on channel '10B' using 'auto' driver, and play with ALSA.
.PP
welle\-pi \-f ./ofdm.iq \-p GRRIF
.IP
Read IQ file './ofdm.iq' (in u8 format) and play programme 'GRIFF' with ALSA.
.PP
welle\-pi \-c 10B \-p GRRIF \-F rtl_tcp,localhost:1234
.IP
Receive 'GRRIF' on channel '10B' using 'rtl_tcp' driver on localhost:1234,
and play with ALSA.
.PP
welle\-pi \-b \-l /var/log/welle\-pi.log \-k /run/welle\-pi.pid \-c 10B \-p GRRIF
.IP
Same as above, but in the background, logging to a file.
